    "message": {
      "content": "# Validation Checklist for Multi-Node Language-Model Serving Systems\n\n## Purpose and Scope\n\nThis checklist validates that a distributed LLM serving system (tensor-parallel, pipeline-parallel, expert-parallel, or data-parallel sharding across nodes) behaves correctly under controlled test conditions. It is designed to catch silent failures \u2014 partial participation, stale configurations, dropped or duplicated requests, and timing artifacts \u2014 that single-node testing cannot expose.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Configuration Identity\n\n**Goal:** Prove every node is running the same logical system.\n\n- [ ] **Model artifact hash.** Record SHA-256 of model weights, tokenizer files, and config files on *every* node. All hashes must match. Do not rely on \"same path\" or \"same version string\" \u2014 verify bytes.\n- [ ] **Code/build identity.** Record git commit, build timestamp, and container image digest per node. Flag any node where the image digest differs, even if the tag is identical.\n- [ ] **Sharding plan agreement.** Each rank must report its assigned layer ranges, tensor-parallel shard indices, and expert assignments. Cross-check that the union of reported assignments exactly covers the model with no gaps or overlaps.\n- [ ] **Deterministic-seed parity.** If sampling temperature > 0, verify all nodes use the same RNG seeding scheme and that sampling happens on a single designated rank (not independently per rank).\n- [ ] **Runtime configuration diff.** Dump effective runtime config (not just the config file \u2014 resolved values after env vars, CLI overrides, and defaults) from each node and diff them. Env-var drift between nodes is a common silent failure.\n- [ ] **Version skew tolerance.** Explicitly document which components may legitimately differ (e.g., driver versions) and which may not (e.g., collective library versions). Anything in the \"may not\" column must be byte-identical.\n\n**Failure signature to watch for:** one node silently",
      "reasoning": "",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
